  "result": "I've written the revised record for NRS_484B_270_7b to `record.jsonl`; it hasn't been through the gate yet. The gate refused the rule with `UNCLAIMED_ATOM` on four atoms. The obligation reads them to find where the pass begins, but no element claimed them.\n\n**Why the fix belongs in the record.** `drv.interaction.overtake_pass` only holds at the moment the pass is recognized. So the rule has to find the pass's beginning itself, using the same definition the concept's contract gives: the motor vehicle is ahead of the subject, their bodies don't overlap lengthwise, and their headings point the same way. The coder was right not to work around this. The only rule possible with the old claims would require safety over the whole window. That is a stricter duty, and it would turn the planned `branch_4` scenario (close following before the pass, then compliant) into a violation.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **y2 now claims the four atoms:** `kin.position`, `kin.heading`, `rel.longitudinal_overlap` and `rel.same_direction`. The justification cites the concept's own wording for the act's beginning. `rel.same_direction` uses the same `p.overtake_same_direction_cos` tolerance the concept is called with.\n- **The obligation text** now locates the beginning by the subject's heading and the two positions, matching the claimed atoms and the coder's rule, instead of naming `rel.bearing`, which nothing claimed. It also states the reading plainly: safe at the beginning and at every observation after it, up to recognition. It adds that a missing position or heading leaves the verdict unknown.\n- **The `idle` scenario** now uses a moped instead of a car, following the coder's note. Under the run's reading a car's membership in these aggregates is unknown rather than false, so a car can't produce `not_applicable`. All three definitions leave a moped out.\n\nNothing else changed: the spans, the standard's operationalization, the parameters, the occasion and the other seven scenarios are as planned. The coder's existing rule and witnesses should now pass the claim check. Whether they pass the rest of the gate won't be known until it is run.",
